Reality itself has no place in NetHack -- realism, on the other hand,
can certainly have some place if it adds to the gameplay value somehow.

> Perhaps "intuition" is a better word than "reality". But since our 
> intuition is based on reality, what difference does it make?

Our intuition WRT Nethack, however, is _not_ based on reality; it's
based on the sum total of our experiences with others' fictional fantasy
genres, including but not limited to Dungeons and Dragons.

Which doesn't make player-intuitiveness any less of a good reason to
have things be designed a certain way, but it does mean that features
should be added or changed based from _that_ perspective, not from a
solely-reality-based one.  (aka "physics 101")

